{
  "india-sells-world-53-billion-of-fuel": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/32/Jamnagar_Refinery.jpg\" alt=\"Aerial view of the Jamnagar oil refinery complex in Gujarat, India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">India's $53 billion in annual refined-fuel exports flows largely from mega-refineries like Reliance's Jamnagar complex, the world's largest. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jamnagar_Refinery.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jamnagar Refinery.jpg</a>, Reliance Industries, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "indias-ev-market-single-digit": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Electric_rickshaw_in_Meerut%2C_Uttar_Pradesh%2C_India.jpg/960px-Electric_rickshaw_in_Meerut%2C_Uttar_Pradesh%2C_India.jpg\" alt=\"An electric rickshaw (e-rickshaw) on a street in Meerut, Uttar Pradesh, India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Electric three-wheelers, like this e-rickshaw in Meerut, have already crossed the tipping point on unsubsidised economics that two-wheelers and cars have not. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Electric_rickshaw_in_Meerut,_Uttar_Pradesh,_India.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Electric rickshaw in Meerut, Uttar Pradesh, India.jpg</a>, Libreravi, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "the-battery-passport-was-built-for": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Lithium-Ion_Battery_for_BMW_i3_-_Battery_Pack.JPG/960px-Lithium-Ion_Battery_for_BMW_i3_-_Battery_Pack.JPG\" alt=\"An exposed lithium-ion battery pack from a BMW i3 electric vehicle\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">A lithium-ion EV battery pack — precisely the object India's battery-passport and fire-safety registries both need to trace but currently cannot. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lithium-Ion_Battery_for_BMW_i3_-_Battery_Pack.JPG\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lithium-Ion Battery for BMW i3 - Battery Pack.JPG</a>, RudolfSimon, CC BY-SA 3.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "where-india-actually-burns-its-fuel": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Petrol_pump%2C_Nagpur%2C_India.jpg/960px-Petrol_pump%2C_Nagpur%2C_India.jpg\" alt=\"A petrol pump station in Nagpur, Maharashtra, India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">A petrol pump in Nagpur, Maharashtra — one of the twelve states that together burn nearly three-quarters of India's petroleum products. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Petrol_pump,_Nagpur,_India.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Petrol pump, Nagpur, India.jpg</a>, Ganesh Dhamodkar, CC BY 1.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "india-environmental-clearances-state": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Singareni_opencast_coal_mines_at_Manuguru_02.jpg/960px-Singareni_opencast_coal_mines_at_Manuguru_02.jpg\" alt=\"Singareni opencast coal mines at Manuguru, Telangana, India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Large opencast mining projects like this one are exactly the kind of proposal that moves through India's Environmental and Wildlife Clearance pipeline. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Singareni_opencast_coal_mines_at_Manuguru_02.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Singareni opencast coal mines at Manuguru 02.jpg</a>, Adityamadhav83, CC BY-SA 3.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "raising-green-debt-globally-rec-euroyen": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Solar_Panels_in_Farm%2C_India.jpg/960px-Solar_Panels_in_Farm%2C_India.jpg\" alt=\"Solar panels installed on a farm in India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Solar power is one of the renewable-energy categories funded by REC Limited's certified green bonds, alongside wind, biogas and pumped storage. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solar_Panels_in_Farm,_India.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Solar Panels in Farm, India.jpg</a>, PWRDF, CC BY 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "which-ecb-currencies-are-actually": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Euler-10_Swiss_Franc_banknote_%28front%29.jpg/960px-Euler-10_Swiss_Franc_banknote_%28front%29.jpg\" alt=\"A Swiss franc banknote\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">The Swiss franc carries the biggest policy-rate gap against India of any reachable currency — but also close to double the US dollar's measured volatility against the rupee. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Euler-10_Swiss_Franc_banknote_(front).jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Euler-10 Swiss Franc banknote (front).jpg</a>, Pascal.Tesson, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "indias-state-incentive-war-gujarats": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Ford_India_President_Shows_Secretary_Kerry_Car_Models_As_He_Tours_New_Factory_Amid_Vibrant_Gujarat_Summit_%2816075447589%29.jpg/960px-Ford_India_President_Shows_Secretary_Kerry_Car_Models_As_He_Tours_New_Factory_Amid_Vibrant_Gujarat_Summit_%2816075447589%29.jpg\" alt=\"U.S. Secretary of State John Kerry tours a Ford manufacturing plant in Gujarat, India, during the Vibrant Gujarat summit\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Gujarat's manufacturing pitch, showcased here at a Ford plant during the Vibrant Gujarat summit, converts into implemented investment far more consistently than most rival states manage. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ford_India_President_Shows_Secretary_Kerry_Car_Models_As_He_Tours_New_Factory_Amid_Vibrant_Gujarat_Summit_(16075447589).jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ford India President Shows Secretary Kerry Car Models As He Tours New Factory Amid Vibrant Gujarat Summit.jpg</a>, U.S. Department of State, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "pet-recycling-already-cuts-emissions-60": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/A_plastic_bottle_collection_facility_for_recycling.jpg/960px-A_plastic_bottle_collection_facility_for_recycling.jpg\" alt=\"Sorted plastic bottles at a recycling collection facility\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Sorted PET bottles at a collection facility — the kind of informal recovery network India's new Extended Producer Responsibility rules are trying to make traceable. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_plastic_bottle_collection_facility_for_recycling.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">A plastic bottle collection facility for recycling.jpg</a>, DoronDoron, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "where-indias-forex-goes-country": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/28/Jawaharlal_Nehru_Trust_Port.jpg\" alt=\"Container terminal at Jawaharlal Nehru Port, near Mumbai, India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Container traffic at Jawaharlal Nehru Port, near Mumbai — a chokepoint for the trade flows behind India's biggest bilateral deficits. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jawaharlal_Nehru_Trust_Port.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jawaharlal Nehru Trust Port.jpg</a>, Jaxer, CC BY 3.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "up-has-indias-biggest-herd-punjab-has": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Sahiwal_cows_at_the_dairy_unit_attached_to_Bhai_Ram_Singh_Memorial_%28Gurudwara%29_Bhaini_Sahib%2C_Ludhyana_%2CPunjab%2C_India.JPG/960px-Sahiwal_cows_at_the_dairy_unit_attached_to_Bhai_Ram_Singh_Memorial_%28Gurudwara%29_Bhaini_Sahib%2C_Ludhyana_%2CPunjab%2C_India.JPG\" alt=\"Sahiwal breed dairy cows at a dairy unit in Ludhiana, Punjab, India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Sahiwal cows at a dairy unit in Ludhiana, Punjab — the state with India's highest milk yield per animal despite a herd far smaller than Uttar Pradesh's. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sahiwal_cows_at_the_dairy_unit_attached_to_Bhai_Ram_Singh_Memorial_(Gurudwara)_Bhaini_Sahib,_Ludhyana_,Punjab,_India.JPG\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sahiwal cows at the dairy unit attached to Bhai Ram Singh Memorial, Bhaini Sahib, Ludhyana, Punjab, India.JPG</a>, Harvinder Chandigarh, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "tiffin-meets-thali-10-day-sip-already": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/BSE_-_Bombay_Stock_Exchange_Building.jpg/960px-BSE_-_Bombay_Stock_Exchange_Building.jpg\" alt=\"The Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) building, Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers, Mumbai\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">The Bombay Stock Exchange, home to the roughly 530 stocks that hold 60% of India's total listed market value — every one still priced by the whole share that a ₹10-a-day multi-asset SIP never has to touch. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BSE_-_Bombay_Stock_Exchange_Building.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">BSE - Bombay Stock Exchange Building.jpg</a>, Niyantha Shekhar, CC BY 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  }
}